sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-35> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Changes of form produced by varying rates of growth are the same phenomenon in individual development and in the differences between species; a transformation from one form to another follows the same course whether it happens within a lifetime or over ancestral history, which accounts for much of von Baer's law of recapitulation.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Form changes follow the same route in individual development and racial history";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Conclusion and summary”. Scope: ontogeny and phylogeny of organic form"
}
